### H1: Greeks V2 flag ramp to 100% overloaded the Monte-Carlo calculator in pricing-engine
cfg-3120 raised flags.pricing.greeks_v2.rollout_pct from 5 to 100 at 12:04:00Z, routing effectively all quote traffic through the GreeksV2 Monte-Carlo calculator (20000 paths). At 5% rollout that path had only ~1/20th the concurrent work; at 100% the pinning of pricing-engine CPU to ~99% shows the calculator is CPU-bound and the full-traffic load exceeds provisioned CPU, so each Monte-Carlo computation stretches to 3-8.9s, blowing the 2000ms quote deadline. pricing-engine p99 jumps from ~60ms to ~2.6s and returns slow/failed quotes; order-service, whose quote call has a 2500ms timeout, times out and its error rate goes from ~0.2% to ~8%.

